egener\u0027s autoantigen","leukocyte proteinase 3","proteinase 3"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.21.76","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins, including elastin, by preferential cleavage:-Ala-|-Xaa- \u003e -Val-|-Xaa-"],"label":"myeloblastin","obo_id":"EC:3.4.21.76","type":"individual"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.21.78","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["cytotoxic T-lymphocyte proteinase 1"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.21.78","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins, including fibronectin, type IV collagen andnucleolin. Preferential cleavage: -Arg-|-Xaa-, -Lys-|-Xaa- \u003e\u003e -Phe-|-Xaa- in small molecule substrates"],"label":"granzyme A","obo_id":"EC:3.4.21.78","type":"individual"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.22.30","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["papaya peptidase A","papaya peptidase II","papaya proteinase III","papaya proteinase Omega","papaya proteinase Q"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.22.30","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity for peptide bonds, similarto those of papain and chymopapain"],"label":"caricain","obo_id":"EC:3.4.22.30","type":"individual"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.23.32","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Scytalidium aspartic proteinase B"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.23.32","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity, cleaving 24-Phe-|-Phe-25,but not 15-Leu-|-Tyr-16 and 25-Phe-|-Tyr-26 in the B chain of insulin"],"label":"scytalidopepsin B","obo_id":"EC:3.4.23.32","type":"individual"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D010289","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Hyperalimentation, Intravenous","Hyperalimentation, Parenteral","Intravenous Hyperalimentation","Nutrition, Total Parenteral","Parenteral Hyperalimentation","Total Parenteral Nutrition"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D010289","description":["The delivery of nutrients for assimilation and utilization by a patient whose sole source of nutrients is via solutions administered intravenously, subcutaneously, or by some other non-alimentary route. The basic components of TPN solutions are protein hydrolysates or free amino acid mixtures, monosaccharides, and electrolytes. Components are selected for their ability to reverse catabolism, promote anabolism, and build structural proteins."],"label":"Parenteral Nutrition, Total","obo_id":"mesh:D010289","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18127","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["1,5-Diaminopentane","1,5-Pentanediamine","1,5-pentamethylenediamine","Cadaverine","DAPE","PENTANE-1,5-DIAMINE","Pentamethylenediamine","pentane-1,5-diamine"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_18127","description":["An alkane-α,ω-diamine comprising a straight-chain pentane core with amino substitutents at positions 1 and 5. A colourless syrupy liquid diamine with a distinctive unpleasant odour, it is a homologue of putresceine and is formed by the bacterial decarboxylation of lysine that occurs during protein hydrolysis during putrefaction of animal tissue. It is also found in plants such as soyabean."],"label":"cadaverine","obo_id":"CHEBI:18127","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["PENTANE-1,5-DIAMINE","pentane-1,5-diamine"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C115176","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C115176","description":["This gene is involved in protein hydrolysis."],"label":"CELA1 Gene","obo_id":"NCIT:C115176","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["CELA1 Gene","CELA1","Chymotrypsin-Like Elastase Family, Member 1 Gene"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C115178","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C115178","description":["Chymotrypsin-like elastase family member 1 (258 aa, ~28 kDa) is encoded by the human CELA1 gene. This protein is involved in protein hydrolysis."],"label":"Chymotrypsin-Like Elastase Family Member 1","obo_id":"NCIT:C115178","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["CELA1","Chymotrypsin-Like Elastase Family Member 1","EC 3.4.21.36","Elastase 1","Elastase-1","Pancreatic Elastase 1","Pancreatic Elastase-1"]},{"iri":"http://snomed.info/id/441671000124100","ontology_name":"snomed","ontology_prefix":"SNOMED","short_form":"SNOMED_441671000124100","description":[],"label":"Hydrolyzed peptide-based high protein enteral formula (product)","obo_id":"","type":"class"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.21.63","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Aspergillus alkaline proteinase","aspergillopeptidase B"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.21.63","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity, and of Bz-Arg-OEt \u003eAc-Tyr-OEt. Does not hydrolyze peptide amides"],"label":"oryzin","obo_id":"EC:3.4.21.63","type":"class"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.23.25","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Saccharomyces aspartic proteinase","yeast endopeptidase A"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.23.25","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity for peptide bonds. Cleaves-Leu-Leu-|-Val-Tyr- bond in a synthetic substrate. Does not act on estersof Tyr or Arg"],"label":"saccharopepsin","obo_id":"EC:3.4.23.25","type":"class"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.21.63","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Aspergillus alkaline proteinase","aspergillopeptidase B"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.21.63","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity, and of Bz-Arg-OEt \u003eAc-Tyr-OEt. Does not hydrolyze peptide amides"],"label":"oryzin","obo_id":"EC:3.4.21.63","type":"individual"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.23.25","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Saccharomyces aspartic proteinase","yeast endopeptidase A"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.23.25","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity for peptide bonds. Cleaves-Leu-Leu-|-Val-Tyr- bond in a synthetic substrate. Does not act on estersof Tyr or Arg"],"label":"saccharopepsin","obo_id":"EC:3.4.23.25","type":"individual"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.21.64","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Tritirachium album proteinase K","Tritirachium alkaline proteinase","endopeptidase K","proteinase K"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.21.64","description":["Hydrolysis of keratin, and of other proteins with subtilisin-likespecificity. Hydrolyzes peptide amides"],"label":"peptidase K","obo_id":"EC:3.4.21.64","type":"class"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.23.18","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Protease type XIII","aspergillopepsin A","aspergillopepsin F","aspergillopeptidase A","awamorin","proctase B","proteinase B","trypsinogen kinase"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.23.18","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity. Generally favorshydrophobic residues in P1 and P1\u0027, but also accepts Lys in P1, whichleads to activation of trypsinogen. Does not clot milk"],"label":"aspergillopepsin I","obo_id":"EC:3.4.23.18","type":"class"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.21.64","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Tritirachium album proteinase K","Tritirachium alkaline proteinase","endopeptidase K","proteinase K"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.21.64","description":["Hydrolysis of keratin, and of other proteins with subtilisin-likespecificity. Hydrolyzes peptide amides"],"label":"peptidase K","obo_id":"EC:3.4.21.64","type":"individual"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.23.18","ontology_name":"ec","related_synonyms":["Protease type XIII","aspergillopepsin A","aspergillopepsin F","aspergillopeptidase A","awamorin","proctase B","proteinase B","trypsinogen kinase"],"ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.23.18","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity. Generally favorshydrophobic residues in P1 and P1\u0027, but also accepts Lys in P1, whichleads to activation of trypsinogen. Does not clot milk"],"label":"aspergillopepsin I","obo_id":"EC:3.4.23.18","type":"individual"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0006508","ontology_name":"go","ontology_prefix":"GO","short_form":"GO_0006508","description":["This term was intentionally placed under \u0027protein metabolic process ; GO:0019538\u0027 rather than \u0027protein catabolic process ; GO:0030163\u0027 to cover all processes centered on breaking peptide bonds, including those involved in protein processing.","The hydrolysis of proteins into smaller polypeptides and/or amino acids by cleavage of their peptide bonds."],"narrow_synonyms":["ATP-dependent proteolysis"],"label":"proteolysis","obo_id":"GO:0006508","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["peptidolysis"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001421","ontology_name":"fypo","related_synonyms":["abnormal protein cleavage during vegetative growth","abnormal protein processing during mitotic cell cycle"],"ontology_prefix":"FYPO","short_form":"FYPO_0001421","description":["We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.","A cellular process phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which protein processing is abnormal. Protein processing is the cleavage of one or more bonds within a protein that leads to the formation of mature, fully functional protein."],"label":"abnormal protein processing during vegetative growth","obo_id":"FYPO:0001421","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["abnormal protein maturation by peptide bond cleavage during vegetative growth","abnormal protein maturation by peptide bond hydrolysis during vegetative growth"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001422","ontology_name":"fypo","related_synonyms":["decreased protein cleavage during vegetative growth","decreased protein processing during mitotic cell cycle"],"ontology_prefix":"FYPO","short_form":"FYPO_0001422","description":["We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.","A cellular metabolism phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the observed occurrence of protein processing is decreased."],"narrow_synonyms":["decreased Sre1 cleavage"],"label":"decreased protein processing during vegetative growth","obo_id":"FYPO:0001422","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["decreased protein maturation by peptide bond cleavage during vegetative growth","decreased protein maturation by peptide bond hydrolysis during vegetative growth","reduced protein processing during vegetative growth"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006376","ontology_name":"fypo","related_synonyms":["decreased protein cleavage during nitrogen starvation"],"ontology_prefix":"FYPO","short_form":"FYPO_0006376","description":["We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.","A cellular metabolism phenotype in which the observed occurrence of protein processing is decreased when the cell is subject to nitrogen starvation."],"label":"decreased protein processing during nitrogen starvation","obo_id":"FYPO:0006376","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["decreased protein maturation by peptide bond cleavage during nitrogen starvation","decreased protein maturation by peptide bond hydrolysis during nitrogen starvation","decreased protein processing during nitrogen depletion","decreased protein processing during nitrogen deprivation","reduced protein processing during nitrogen starvation"]},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.24.63","ontology_name":"ec","ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.24.63","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins, including azocasein, and peptides. Hydrolysis of5-His-|-Leu-6, 6-Leu-|-Cys-7, 14-Ala-|-Leu-15 and 19-Cys-|-Gly-20 bondsin insulin B chain"],"label":"meprin B","obo_id":"EC:3.4.24.63","type":"class"},{"iri":"https://www.enzyme-database.org/query.php?ec\u003d3.4.24.63","ontology_name":"ec","ontology_prefix":"EC","short_form":"EC_3.4.24.63","description":["Hydrolysis of proteins, including azocasein, and peptides. Hydrolysis of5-His-|-Leu-6, 6-Leu-|-Cys-7, 14-Ala-|-Leu-15 and 19-Cys-|-Gly-20 bondsin insulin B chain"],"label":"meprin B","obo_id":"EC:3.4.24.63","type":"individual"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0051725","ontology_name":"go","ontology_prefix":"GO","short_form":"GO_0051725","description":["The process of removing one or more ADP-ribose residues from a protein."],"label":"protein de-ADP-ribosylation","obo_id":"GO:0051725","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["poly(ADP-ribose) removal from protein","protein poly(ADP-ribose) catabolic process","protein poly(ADP-ribose) catabolism","protein poly(ADP-ribose) degradation","protein poly(ADP-ribose) hydrolysis","removal of ADP-ribose from protein","protein amino acid de-ADP-ribosylation"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006374","ontology_name":"fypo","related_synonyms":["abnormal protein cleavage"],"ontology_prefix":"FYPO","short_form":"FYPO_0006374","description":["We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term.","A cellular process phenotype in which protein processing is abnormal. Protein processing is the cleavage of one or more bonds within a protein that leads to the formation of mature, fully functional protein."],"label":"abnormal protein processing","obo_id":"FYPO:0006374","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["abnormal protein maturation by peptide bond cleavage","abnormal protein maturation by peptide bond hydrolysis"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C92657","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C92657","description":["Carboxypeptidase Q (472 aa, ~52 kDa) is encoded by the human CPQ gene. This protein plays a role in the hydrolysis of proteins and circulating peptides."],"label":"Carboxypeptidase Q","obo_id":"NCIT:C92657","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Blood Plasma Glutamate Carboxypeptidase","CPQ","Carboxypeptidase Q","EC 3.4.17.-","Lysosomal Dipeptidase","Plasma Glutamate Carboxypeptidase","Ser-Met Dipeptidase"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D010446","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Fragment, Peptide","Fragments, Peptide","Peptide Fragment"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D010446","description":["Partial proteins formed by partial hydrolysis of complete proteins or generated through PROTEIN ENGINEERING techniques."],"label":"Peptide Fragments","obo_id":"mesh:D010446","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0017090","ontology_name":"go","ontology_prefix":"GO","short_form":"GO_0017090","description":["A protein complex that is located in the cell membrane, and is involved in the metabolism of peptides, including neuropeptides. The complex has metalloendopeptidase activity that catalyzes the hydrolysis of protein and peptide substrates, preferentially on carboxyl side of hydrophobic residues."],"label":"meprin A complex","obo_id":"GO:0017090","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["PABA peptide hydrolase complex"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C13459","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C13459","description":["The portion of a proteolytic protein which causes hydrolysis and cleavage of other protein polypeptides."],"label":"Protease Domain","obo_id":"NCIT:C13459","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Protease Domain","Proteolytic Domain"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D019286","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Alkaline Proteinase, Tritirachium","Protease K","Proteinase K","Proteinase, Tritirachium Alkaline","Tritirachium Alkaline Proteinase"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D019286","de